apc_modbus: fix inverted APC_VF_UNAVAILABLE check in _apc_modbus_setvar()

The NUT 2.8.5 git snapshot (0e051f9) vendored in nut-2.8.5-src.tar.gz
tests the APC_VF_UNAVAILABLE flag with a spurious '!', so every
variable that is actually present is rejected with "is not available"
and STAT_SET_INVALID. upsd still ACKs the SET, so clients see OK while
the UPS never receives the write -- e.g. `upsrw -s battery.date=...`
(and the web UI "Battery Replaced" button) silently does nothing.

The flag is only set for outlet groups absent on the device, so the
check must reject flagged entries, not unflagged ones. Patch is applied
defensively in install.sh if the tarball is ever regenerated from an
unpatched upstream snapshot.

--- a/drivers/apc_modbus.c	2026-10-19 09:57:43.621397667 +0100
+++ b/drivers/apc_modbus.c	2026-10-19 09:57:43.624225882 +0100
@@ -1614,7 +1614,7 @@
 		return STAT_SET_UNKNOWN;
 	}
 
-	if (!(apc_value->value_flags & APC_VF_UNAVAILABLE)) {
+	if ((apc_value->value_flags & APC_VF_UNAVAILABLE)) {
 		upslogx(LOG_SET_INVALID, "%s: [%s] is not available", __func__, nut_varname);
 		return STAT_SET_INVALID;
 	}
